      "object_role": "synthesis",
      "proposed_content": "Two distinct analytic programs compile infinite arithmetic questions into finite coefficient searches. Divisor-weight design is evaluated through an explicit integral-functional quotient and a strict h(c) threshold; zero-free-region design searches admissible trigonometric polynomials, whose coefficient vector must still satisfy global nonnegativity and the target objective. Optimization proposes witnesses only inside these prior analytic interfaces.",
