      "proposed_content": "Weil's test-function formalism converts zero location into sign conditions coupling zero, prime, and archimedean terms. Semi-local quotients, scaling actions, trace formulas, compact support, and moment constraints localize the proposed operator problem, but the same localization omits the global Poisson normalization of principal values; Hilbert-space identification alone therefore does not supply positivity.",
